WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: zh-Hant

00:01:08.672 --> 00:01:09.930
Yo yo, I'm Loot2.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.280
Over the past two months, we've done two rides in the Philippines.

00:01:13.557 --> 00:01:16.900
Both trips were adventures into the mountains and inland areas of the Philippines.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.933
On one hand, it's because we've always loved exploring different places.

00:01:19.933 --> 00:01:22.866
We've always had a strong passion for riding overseas.

00:01:23.066 --> 00:01:25.863
On the other hand, after our first trip back from the Philippines,

00:01:25.863 --> 00:01:26.691
we realized

00:01:26.691 --> 00:01:28.933
a lot of friends were really interested in riding in the Philippines,

00:01:28.933 --> 00:01:32.233
and the level of interest was really high.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.931
So in less than a month,

00:01:33.931 --> 00:01:36.400
we gathered a few friends who had joined us before on our off-road rides,

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:39.100
and also some riding buddies we were more familiar with, to come along.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:43.433
This series will be split into two parts depending on the route.

00:01:43.866 --> 00:01:46.500
The first part focuses on an adventure on ADV bikes.

00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:50.266
It includes water crossings, easy dirt roads, mountain routes, and epic views.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.333
Perfect for people who want to ride and enjoy the scenery

00:01:52.533 --> 00:01:54.860
and experience the local customs and way of life.

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:57.533
The second half will focus on forest-road off-road riding,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.200
led by Marvin, the famous PSBK champion from the Philippines,

00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:02.633
who will guide us on the ride.

00:02:02.633 --> 00:02:05.433
It's for riders who want something a bit more hardcore.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.624
We finally made it to the Philippines alive.

00:02:10.624 --> 00:02:13.850
Yeah~~ riding~~

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:17.418
Let's go~~ GO~~

00:02:17.418 --> 00:02:18.761
Arriving at Manila Airport

00:02:18.761 --> 00:02:20.298
loading our bags onto the luggage cart

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.074
after we got into the van,

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.466
the day before we ride,

00:02:23.466 --> 00:02:25.900
we're going to explore Manila first

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.666
We are going to the Xinyi District in the Philippines

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.233
The Xinyi District in Manila, not the Philippines' Xinyi District.

00:02:39.233 --> 00:02:41.433
Lunch in Manila's Xinyi District.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.433
What do you think about flying to the Philippines in business class?

00:02:43.433 --> 00:02:45.000
So comfortable.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:45.900
I kept falling asleep.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.866
You're seriously so annoying. Like, insanely annoying.

00:02:49.066 --> 00:02:51.466
You kept posting pics the whole way with nobody next to you. So annoying.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.300
If anyone's going to get robbed, rob him. Don't rob us.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.733
We're broke. He's the richest.

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:57.466
Metro Manila

00:02:57.466 --> 00:03:00.333
Its area is about 2.3 times that of Taipei City.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:03.546
Its population is well over 13 million.

00:03:03.733 --> 00:03:05.633
So if you're sitting in a car,

00:03:05.666 --> 00:03:09.100
this is probably the kind of view you'll get, hahaha.

00:03:09.266 --> 00:03:11.100
Traffic jams are just part of daily life here

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.860
A stretch of road under 10 kilometers took 50 minutes

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.413
That's probably still pretty fast, haha.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:16.677
As for the traffic,

00:03:16.677 --> 00:03:19.600
we'll talk more about it once we start riding.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:20.900
And besides the traffic,

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.533
a lot of people, as soon as they hear Manila,

00:03:22.533 --> 00:03:27.266
immediately think of crime, crowds, and chaos.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:29.834
Turning left. We don't give a damn about that Coca-Cola truck.

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:30.933
Is that Coca-Cola truck gonna run into us?

00:03:30.933 --> 00:03:32.733
That Coca-Cola truck doesn't give a damn about us either.

00:03:34.533 --> 00:03:36.333
Motorcycle again, motorcycle again

00:03:37.533 --> 00:03:38.400
There are so many cars beside us

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.200
But we still bravely turned through

00:03:42.633 --> 00:03:44.066
But actually, that impression

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:46.666
only tells part of the story.

00:03:46.666 --> 00:03:47.933
More accurately,

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:52.500
Manila is a big metropolis with many layers and sharp contrasts.

00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:56.266
The old district still has walls and streets left from the colonial era.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:00.666
The traditional commercial areas are full of traffic, crowds, and everyday life.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.800
And in some newer districts,

00:04:02.933 --> 00:04:07.200
the city suddenly puts on a clean, polished face.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.400
BGC is one of those places.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:11.860
Bonifacio

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:12.900
High Street

00:04:13.941 --> 00:04:16.800
Right? Is that how you say it? Bonifacio

00:04:16.866 --> 00:04:18.333
Bonifacio High Street

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.576
The Xinyi District of the Philippines.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.433
The first car we saw in BGC

00:04:22.433 --> 00:04:24.033
was our KTM 390 ADV.

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:24.733
So cool.

00:04:24.866 --> 00:04:29.000
BGC is basically the Xinyi District of Metro Manila.

00:04:29.266 --> 00:04:32.233
The area is well developed, and the streets are clean.

00:04:32.333 --> 00:04:35.000
It feels orderly, and there are lots of shops too.

00:04:35.365 --> 00:04:36.037
And honestly,

00:04:36.037 --> 00:04:38.600
what left the deepest impression on me in BGC

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:40.500
wasn't the rows of skyscrapers,

00:04:40.633 --> 00:04:43.433
but every cat sitting in front of the shops.

00:04:43.666 --> 00:04:44.533
So cute.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:45.600
You little stinky cat.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.100
Stinky cat.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.797
They're so skinny.

00:04:57.266 --> 00:04:59.633
If you love cats and come here,

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:01.931
wow, you'd probably be helpless, haha.

00:05:01.931 --> 00:05:02.805
Once we got to BGC,

00:05:02.805 --> 00:05:04.400
we also had lunch here at noon.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:08.080
We had Manam, Filipino fusion local cuisine.

00:05:08.533 --> 00:05:10.700
Finally, it's time to eat.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.466
We ordered a very generous spread.

00:05:12.466 --> 00:05:13.000
Dig in.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.533
Even though among all the dishes,

00:05:14.533 --> 00:05:16.433
I only knew there was one fried pork knuckle, lol.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.300
But every dish was pretty tasty.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.866
There were no real flavor mismatches.

00:05:20.233 --> 00:05:23.466
My first meal after landing was so filling I was stuffed.

00:05:23.833 --> 00:05:25.433
I was super satisfied.

00:05:25.666 --> 00:05:27.033
Nice to meet you all.

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:28.394
He said that over these three days,

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:29.631
you'll be riding tomorrow,

00:05:29.631 --> 00:05:30.778
are you excited?

00:05:30.949 --> 00:05:32.193
Yeah.

00:05:32.193 --> 00:05:32.962
Pretty excited.

00:05:32.962 --> 00:05:33.621
Yeah.

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.500
This is basically their sacred mountain here in the Philippines.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:40.186
That was pretty much useless info, haha.

00:05:41.114 --> 00:05:42.144
How long is this route?

00:05:42.144 --> 00:05:44.020
300.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:44.928
From here

00:05:45.248 --> 00:05:48.288
going to… about 300.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.300
After lunch, we hung out in BGC for about another hour

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.433
to let the food digest.

00:05:53.533 --> 00:05:55.666
In the afternoon, we headed to Alpinestars in the Philippines.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.233
This stop was just for everyone to do a little shopping,

00:05:58.266 --> 00:06:01.100
like knee pads, elbow guards, chest protectors, or off-road gloves if they'd forgotten any,

00:06:01.333 --> 00:06:03.900
plus riding boots, helmets, and dirt bike jerseys they liked.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.458
You can get everything you need here in one go.

00:06:06.533 --> 00:06:08.931
And since I'd only been here less than two months ago,

00:06:08.931 --> 00:06:10.531
and before this trip,

00:06:10.531 --> 00:06:13.866
I'd also just gone to I Moto to pick up a new pair of riding boots, LAETT 8.5,

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:16.842
I was actually already itching to get going and ride right away

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:19.066
just to test out these new boots, lol.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:22.100
So this time I only bought some gloves and long riding socks,

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:24.362
and the rest was just me trying to convince everyone else to buy stuff, lol.

00:06:26.066 --> 00:06:27.533
After shopping, we got back in the car

00:06:27.533 --> 00:06:31.200
and headed off to meet the group we'd be riding with this time.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.061
After another nearly hour-long drive,

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.666
we finally arrived around 7 p.m.,

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:38.245
we arrived at LABL Café.

00:06:38.266 --> 00:06:42.233
There's music, coffee, and even food here.

00:06:42.866 --> 00:06:43.900
He arranged it all.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.300
and it also includes the entire route for this trip

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.233
he personally rode and scouted out beforehand.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:52.448
Joe

00:06:53.018 --> 00:06:53.786
Anna

00:06:56.352 --> 00:06:58.528
There are 14 people here

00:06:59.034 --> 00:07:01.146
So I'm worried about you, you know?

00:07:02.341 --> 00:07:04.506
We operate a company in Taiwan

00:07:04.506 --> 00:07:08.949
that focuses on dirt biking, so next time you can come and have fun too

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:13.333
LABL is a local outdoor apparel brand in the Philippines.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.300
The boss, Derrick, also has another film production company

00:07:16.466 --> 00:07:18.266
Motorcycle Cinema

00:07:18.266 --> 00:07:21.200
They mainly shoot motorcycle-related ads and videos.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.210
Now they're also starting to put together

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.900
trips for overseas visitors to ride motorcycles in the Philippines.

00:07:26.266 --> 00:07:29.433
This trip was all arranged by them.

00:07:29.872 --> 00:07:32.260
Ready to take us from the capital Manila

00:07:32.266 --> 00:07:35.633
to Tanay in eastern Luzon for an adventure,

00:07:35.733 --> 00:07:38.700
with a support van and a film crew following along.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:40.133
So in this video,

00:07:40.233 --> 00:07:42.133
quite a lot of the footage

00:07:42.133 --> 00:07:44.200
was shot by Motorcycle Cinema.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:46.000
While keeping the production value high,

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.762
I can also focus more on enjoying

00:07:47.762 --> 00:07:49.573
the countryside roads in the Philippines, hahaha.

00:07:51.733 --> 00:07:55.930
Very good, very nice

00:07:57.466 --> 00:07:59.700
And one thing that really stood out to me here

00:07:59.933 --> 00:08:02.466
was the origin of the name LABL,

00:08:02.533 --> 00:08:05.433
which is also the vision Derrick and his team had when starting the brand:

00:08:05.633 --> 00:08:07.500
Living A Balanced Life

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:08.931
Your life should be balanced,

00:08:08.931 --> 00:08:11.056
not just work, and not just play.

00:08:11.056 --> 00:08:12.200
It's all about balancing your life.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.651
After we got to LABL,

00:08:13.651 --> 00:08:15.322
we saw the bikes we'd be riding this time.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:19.706
The 450 MT, and Royal Enfield's Himalayan 450.

00:08:19.733 --> 00:08:23.731
Honestly, the Himalayan 450 looks even better than I expected.

00:08:23.731 --> 00:08:26.112
Yeah, I thought it would be smaller.

00:08:26.112 --> 00:08:28.200
Yeah, it looks better than I expected.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.900
We took some time to check out the bikes here, then had dinner.

00:08:30.981 --> 00:08:36.103
After dinner, there was a brief briefing for the two-day, one-night trip.

00:08:36.103 --> 00:08:39.543
First, I'll go over tomorrow's itinerary.

00:08:39.543 --> 00:08:44.720
Tomorrow, we're setting off from here.

00:08:45.461 --> 00:08:47.584
We pick up the bikes at 4:00 a.m.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:50.464
So we need to be here by 3:00 a.m., 3:30 a.m.

00:08:50.874 --> 00:08:51.904
We have a team

00:08:51.904 --> 00:08:54.066
that will film you if you drop your bike — for memories, LOL.

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:58.234
A motorcycle mechanic will also be riding along.

00:08:58.234 --> 00:09:00.448
So you don't end up crashing around everywhere, XD.

00:09:00.448 --> 00:09:02.864
They can fix it on the spot.

00:09:02.864 --> 00:09:06.033
After the briefing, we took the shuttle back to the hotel and got ready to rest.

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:08.060
We're getting ready for tomorrow's trip.

00:09:11.274 --> 00:09:11.984
Everyone,

00:09:12.266 --> 00:09:14.600
Honestly, I'm not sure if you can even see my face right now.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:17.231
The time now is 3:15 a.m.

00:09:17.231 --> 00:09:20.058
It's 3:15 in the morning, and we're all fully geared up.

00:09:20.058 --> 00:09:21.866
And we just loaded our luggage onto the vehicle.

00:09:21.933 --> 00:09:25.300
When we got to the hotel yesterday, it was already close to 11 p.m.

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:28.600
After taking a shower and organizing our things,

00:09:28.633 --> 00:09:30.131
we got up again around 2:30.

00:09:30.131 --> 00:09:31.091
And now it's 3:00.

00:09:31.091 --> 00:09:34.841
So we're heading over to LABL to pick up our bikes.

00:09:34.841 --> 00:09:36.746
Why is day one starting so early?

00:09:36.746 --> 00:09:38.300
Because we're going to catch the sunrise.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:41.333
Then wait a minute, we'll go to 7-11 to resupply first

00:09:41.333 --> 00:09:43.100
Apparently, the first thing to do is grab a Red Bull,

00:09:43.333 --> 00:09:44.333
and chug it right away.

00:09:44.533 --> 00:09:45.800
Otherwise, we're seriously about to crash.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:48.933
After leaving our lodging,

00:09:48.933 --> 00:09:50.231
we finally made it to 7-Eleven.

00:09:50.231 --> 00:09:54.453
A source of energy—breakfast. Breakfast is a must.

00:09:54.453 --> 00:09:57.800
Everyone headed straight for the energy drink aisle.

00:10:02.233 --> 00:10:03.033
Everyone,

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:06.266
we're in a foreign country, but we still need to refuel.

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:10.600
Even though we didn't sleep much, these four cans in my hand,

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:13.666
I'm sure they'll keep me energized all day long.

00:10:14.533 --> 00:10:17.466
The source of energy for the whole day, LIPOVITAM

00:10:17.466 --> 00:10:18.733
Drink it and you'll feel instantly energized

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:22.260
Right now, we're just downing it

00:10:25.733 --> 00:10:27.063
After buying the energy drinks,

00:10:27.063 --> 00:10:30.464
the whole team's 14 headsets were connected by MESH,

00:10:30.464 --> 00:10:31.866
we were ready to set off.

00:10:48.933 --> 00:10:51.833
After setting off, we first stopped at a gas station to fill up.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:53.146
Every time I ride overseas,

00:10:53.146 --> 00:10:56.066
I feel that before setting off, stopping at a gas station to top off the tank

00:10:56.133 --> 00:10:58.700
has already become an essential ritual.

00:10:59.033 --> 00:11:00.900
After filling up, we officially set off,

00:11:01.024 --> 00:11:02.830
ready to enter the first checkpoint.

00:11:02.933 --> 00:11:06.000
In downtown Manila at a little after 4 a.m.

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:13.594
Once I got on the bike,

00:11:13.594 --> 00:11:14.794
first, I have to talk about

00:11:14.794 --> 00:11:18.033
my thoughts on wearing the new Leatt 8.5 boots.

00:11:18.266 --> 00:11:20.266
Ever since I first got into dirt bikes,

00:11:20.266 --> 00:11:23.500
I've always worn riding boots from LEATT, the South African brand.

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.896
I started with the 5.5 and am already on my second pair.

00:11:27.173 --> 00:11:30.442
Recently, they also released the new 6.5 and 8.5 models.

00:11:32.746 --> 00:11:34.608
The 6.5 features a full sole design,

00:11:34.608 --> 00:11:36.112
with more complete protection overall,

00:11:36.112 --> 00:11:37.530
and a more secure, wrapped-around fit.

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:40.333
It's better suited for long periods of standing while riding,

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:43.400
and for riding situations with more impact and strain,

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:45.029
like hard enduro routes.

00:11:45.333 --> 00:11:47.100
As for the Leatt 8.5 I wore this time,

00:11:47.133 --> 00:11:49.433
its positioning leans more toward an ADV boot.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:51.242
It's not the kind of boot that,

00:11:51.242 --> 00:11:54.033
instantly makes you feel like today is a fight to the finish.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:56.600
Instead of just protecting you,

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:58.400
it strikes a really good balance

00:11:58.866 --> 00:12:00.300
for anyone who needs to ride all day

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:02.700
and go from asphalt to gravel to dirt roads,

00:12:03.066 --> 00:12:06.333
even getting off the bike and walking a short distance in between,

00:12:06.333 --> 00:12:08.200
that kind of balance is really important.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.600
What stood out to me most about these boots

00:12:10.633 --> 00:12:14.200
was that they removed the top buckle around the calf.

00:12:14.466 --> 00:12:15.800
It doesn't look like a big change,

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:17.866
but once you actually put them on, it makes a huge difference.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.218
With some riding boots, it's not the foot that's the problem,

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:22.200
it's that your calf just won't fit in,

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.033
or if you force it in,

00:12:24.133 --> 00:12:26.633
the buckle feels tight and uncomfortable all day.

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:30.066
But the 8.5 is much more forgiving in that area.

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:32.291
If you're interested in the 6.5 or 8.5,

00:12:32.291 --> 00:12:34.208
you can also try them on at E-Moto.

00:12:34.426 --> 00:12:35.120
And as far as I know,

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:37.466
we had to get up very early for this trip.

00:12:37.533 --> 00:12:39.266
There were two main reasons.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:42.700
First, so we could reach the mountains before 6:30 a.m.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.300
to catch the beautiful sunrise in the Philippines.

00:12:45.533 --> 00:12:48.066
And the second was, I think, the biggest reason of all.

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:52.021
That was to avoid the rush-hour traffic.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.033
Manila at 4 a.m.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:57.033
had a lot more traffic than we expected.

00:12:57.133 --> 00:12:58.400
Looking back now,

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:00.580
it's only about 2.3 times the size of Taipei City,

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:03.104
yet it has to pack in over 13 million people.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:06.197
So yeah, it kind of has to be crowded.

00:13:06.368 --> 00:13:07.290
And just stepping out the door

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:09.833
you were immediately in this high-density traffic environment.

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:12.400
That gave me a few very direct takeaways

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:15.233
about riding in the Philippines very quickly.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:17.100
And if you ever come to Manila,

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:20.033
you really have to take a ride through downtown Manila.

00:13:20.133 --> 00:13:21.300
It's genuinely a lot of fun.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:23.274
First, for me personally,

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:25.333
there's really no need to hold back on the horn, lol.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:28.533
Whether you want to overtake, change lanes,

00:13:28.666 --> 00:13:30.833
or squeeze through a gap to get ahead,

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.333
just hit it.

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:33.561
Because here,

00:13:33.561 --> 00:13:35.498
the horn is almost never about anger.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.500
It's not scolding people or starting a fight.

00:13:50.133 --> 00:13:51.666
The most dangerous situation

00:13:51.666 --> 00:13:54.500
usually isn't someone who's super decisive and clear,

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:57.133
but someone who's half-overtaking, half-changing lanes,

00:13:57.260 --> 00:13:59.994
moving hesitantly with no clear signal.

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:01.818
Because in this kind of traffic flow,

00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:04.725
everyone is really just moving by reading each other's intentions.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:06.266
As long as you honk,

00:14:06.266 --> 00:14:08.033
or even flash your high beams a little,

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.433
most people will understand what you mean

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:13.666
and usually make room for you to pass.

00:14:13.933 --> 00:14:15.900
But if you don't signal at all,

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.833
others will actually assume,

00:14:17.866 --> 00:14:19.566
"Are you letting me go first?"

00:14:19.733 --> 00:14:22.033
Then you yield, I yield, and everyone's guessing.

00:14:22.233 --> 00:14:24.900
That moment is the most jammed up—and the easiest to mess up.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:26.346
So what was interesting was

00:14:26.346 --> 00:14:28.800
that after a group of riders from Taiwan got here,

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.629
we had originally thought we'd have a really hard time adjusting,

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:33.466
but as we kept riding, we actually started to feel that

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:35.733
riding through downtown Manila

00:14:35.733 --> 00:14:37.800
had this indescribable thrill to it.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:39.733
It's even a bit fun, XDDDD.

00:14:39.733 --> 00:14:42.833
Everyone basically earned their "Philippine driver's license" just from surviving that traffic, lol.

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:45.637
I freaking love the Philippines.

00:14:50.122 --> 00:14:51.632
5:58 a.m.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:55.200
Sunrise is at 6:04, six minutes to go.

00:14:55.933 --> 00:14:56.666
Finally,

00:14:56.666 --> 00:15:00.131
for our morning warm-up stretch, we rode for nearly two hours

00:15:00.131 --> 00:15:02.714
from the city into the mountains.

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:10.133
Look over there.

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:14.160
That's Sierra Madre, a mountain range.

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:15.824
It's basically the Philippines' version of the Central Mountain Range

00:15:15.824 --> 00:15:19.904
that helps break up typhoons heading for Manila,

00:15:19.904 --> 00:15:20.330
Yeah.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:21.940
protecting the country from even more typhoons.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:24.931
Taiwan has one too!

00:15:24.931 --> 00:15:25.946
It's beautiful!

00:15:27.133 --> 00:15:31.000
We've now come to the Philippines' version of the nation's sacred mountain.

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:34.506
Once typhoons hit this mountain on their way to the Philippines,

00:15:34.506 --> 00:15:36.100
they usually weaken a lot.

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:39.033
We got into the mountains before 6:30 a.m.

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:42.640
so we could catch the Philippines' slightly warm

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:44.650
yet surprisingly gentle sunrise.

00:15:44.866 --> 00:15:47.833
This sunrise is more than just "the sun coming up."

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:51.133
It's when you ride out of the city while it's still half asleep

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:54.618
and watch the sky slowly fade from deep blue to orange-gold.

00:15:54.733 --> 00:15:56.233
You can really feel

00:15:56.433 --> 00:15:58.733
that today's journey has truly begun.

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:05.233
We'll be in there in a bit. We're going in.

00:16:05.233 --> 00:16:09.463
There'll be some rivers, just a little bit of river.

00:16:09.463 --> 00:16:12.392
The uphill stretch still has plenty of surprises.

00:16:12.392 --> 00:16:13.712
Thank you.

00:16:14.517 --> 00:16:15.754
Cheers. Iced Americano!!!

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:21.133
We've been riding for about an hour now.

00:16:21.133 --> 00:16:23.800
I think from what you just saw on screen, you could probably feel it too

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:25.200
that it was a chaotic hour

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:28.722
because downtown Manila is really intense.

00:16:28.722 --> 00:16:31.063
I even feel like riding in the city

00:16:31.063 --> 00:16:33.282
is more fun than riding in the mountains.

00:16:33.282 --> 00:16:34.271
This time, when we set out,

00:16:34.271 --> 00:16:36.336
everyone had Bluetooth headsets mounted on their helmets.

00:16:36.336 --> 00:16:38.633
As we rode, we'd share road conditions

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:40.064
and talk about our own impressions.

00:16:40.064 --> 00:16:42.933
Do you think riding from the city here was fun?

00:16:44.233 --> 00:16:45.233
Chaos, but orderly.

00:16:45.233 --> 00:16:47.000
Skill comes first.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:47.834
Courage comes second.

00:16:47.834 --> 00:16:51.066
And luck plays a part too—luck is third.

00:16:52.789 --> 00:16:54.341
No rules. You are the rule.

00:16:54.341 --> 00:16:55.700
You're the one making the rules.

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.800
It's like weaving through that jungle.

00:16:57.800 --> 00:16:59.931
So it feels like you're riding the Batmobile,

00:16:59.931 --> 00:17:00.250
Yeah, yeah.

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:02.600
and all kinds of random stuff all around you.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:03.766
And then you're basically playing above your level.

00:17:04.026 --> 00:17:05.730
Just ride however you want—squeeze through wherever you can.

00:17:05.733 --> 00:17:07.500
Once you get here, you become a Filipino.

00:17:08.066 --> 00:17:10.333
Seriously, they're honking like crazy.

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:11.200
Isn't this awesome?

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.600
The city is better than the mountain roads.

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:15.968
Even though there are a lot of cars, I never feel like I'm stuck in traffic.

00:17:15.968 --> 00:17:16.466
Exactly.

00:17:16.466 --> 00:17:17.466
I get more and more excited the more I ride.

00:17:17.466 --> 00:17:19.700
Riding in the city here really feels like playing a game.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:20.837
It's chaotic, though.

00:17:20.837 --> 00:17:23.433
But when it comes to watching the road,

00:17:23.766 --> 00:17:24.731
they really do keep an eye out.

00:17:24.731 --> 00:17:27.873
You won't get that kind of left turn where they just ignore us.

00:17:27.873 --> 00:17:29.349
Seeing the sunrise also made me feel like

00:17:29.349 --> 00:17:31.033
on the first day of this trip,

00:17:31.266 --> 00:17:34.466
waking up that early was really worth it.

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:37.690
After breakfast here, we were ready to keep going.

00:17:42.566 --> 00:17:46.400
Breakfast's done. Time to head out again.

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:48.293
Apparently, after setting off from here,

00:17:48.293 --> 00:17:51.333
we'd ride about 15 more minutes on concrete.

00:17:51.433 --> 00:17:54.163
Then we'd get onto unpaved roads.

00:17:54.163 --> 00:17:55.749
Ready to go. Go, go.

00:17:55.749 --> 00:17:58.233
Our guide for this trip is Joseph.

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:00.266
Joseph, nice to meet you.

00:18:00.394 --> 00:18:01.674
Nice to meet you.

00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:06.992
After about 20 minutes of riding,

00:19:06.992 --> 00:19:09.333
we left the paved road and turned onto a small trail.

00:19:09.509 --> 00:19:12.160
We'd finally reached the unpaved section.

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:14.400
I was instantly fired up.

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:17.000
What stood out to me most about this stretch

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:18.768
were the sections where we forded through water.

00:19:19.125 --> 00:19:19.888
The terrain here

00:19:19.888 --> 00:19:23.066
immediately reminded me of the Wulaokeng Forest Trail in Yilan.

00:19:23.466 --> 00:19:26.466
This whole road isn't just a dirt track or a rocky path.

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.833
Streams keep cutting across the forest road here.

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:32.128
Along the stream, there are also little bridges you can take to bypass it.

00:19:32.366 --> 00:19:34.800
But since we're already here, the bridges and all

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.900
can wait until we have time to come back, haha.

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:38.266
The first stream crossing wasn't very deep.

00:19:38.266 --> 00:19:40.266
It was only a little above ankle height.

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:43.800
Normally, that kind of depth shouldn't be too intimidating.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.653
But when you actually ride into it,

00:19:45.653 --> 00:19:48.100
your heart still starts pounding honestly.

00:19:48.266 --> 00:19:50.566
It feels like all your senses suddenly switch on.

00:19:50.768 --> 00:19:53.330
The adrenaline starts to rise without you even noticing.

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:56.000
These river-crossing sections are actually pretty flat.

00:19:56.133 --> 00:19:57.500
We just kept riding along this road.

00:19:57.530 --> 00:20:00.538
We were riding through rivers and over unpaved roads.

00:20:00.733 --> 00:20:03.366
The whole ride was actually really relaxing.

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:06.733
Especially once we got to the dirt sections, the conditions were fantastic.

00:20:06.733 --> 00:20:08.966
Riding an ADV bike to a place like this

00:20:09.233 --> 00:20:11.666
really lets you enjoy its most appealing side.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:13.366
You don't have to be like you are on the highway,

00:20:13.366 --> 00:20:15.266
just trying to get the distance done.

00:20:15.566 --> 00:20:17.763
And it's not like being in some hardcore terrain,

00:20:17.763 --> 00:20:19.408
where you're dealing with obstacles every second.

00:20:19.482 --> 00:20:21.301
This place sits right between the two.

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:24.600
It has a bit of adventure, but still plenty of ease.

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:25.731
Before you know it,

00:20:25.731 --> 00:20:29.509
we were also fully in the mindset of an off-road trip.

00:20:29.633 --> 00:20:31.431
You start losing track of time.

00:20:31.431 --> 00:20:34.234
You forget the noise and crowds from the city.

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:38.032
All that's left in front of you is the road, the river, and the mountains.

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:42.394
And the bike carrying you deeper and deeper along the way.

00:20:57.966 --> 00:20:59.200
As we kept moving forward,

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:01.566
we left the dirt road and returned to pavement.

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:03.631
In the end, we rode for nearly an hour and a half

00:21:03.631 --> 00:21:06.864
and arrived at our lunch spot, Danalak Falls.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:09.842
The waterfall itself isn't one of those massive,

00:21:09.842 --> 00:21:11.482
overwhelming ones.

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:15.968
It's more like a cool, shaded corner tucked away in the mountains.

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:18.405
Water pours down from the rock wall

00:21:18.566 --> 00:21:22.300
and falls into a pool below with a slight blue-green tint,

00:21:22.437 --> 00:21:24.160
surrounded by trees.

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:25.802
The whole place felt really comfortable.

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:29.472
It made you want to just sit down and zone out for a bit.

00:21:52.533 --> 00:21:54.233
After eating and drinking our fill here at the waterfall,

00:21:54.233 --> 00:21:55.233
we set off again.

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:57.733
After about 20 minutes on the highway,

00:21:57.733 --> 00:22:00.133
we came to another trail junction.

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:01.370
We turned right here

00:22:01.370 --> 00:22:02.931
and prepared to head straight toward this

00:22:02.931 --> 00:22:05.856
mountaintop spot, which I thought had absolutely amazing views.

00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:26.900
After turning right, this trail

00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:29.781
felt like the whole world suddenly switched.

00:22:30.233 --> 00:22:33.133
The road started narrowing, and the trees got denser,

00:22:33.400 --> 00:22:35.568
and there was still a bit of moisture in the air.

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:38.233
And what left the deepest impression on me here was

00:22:38.466 --> 00:22:40.133
because this is an ADV route,

00:22:40.133 --> 00:22:41.933
so from this morning until now,

00:22:42.100 --> 00:22:44.600
the roads we've taken haven't really been that difficult,

00:22:44.900 --> 00:22:46.833
at least from a local's point of view.

00:22:47.200 --> 00:22:49.733
These probably all still count as "normal roads."

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:51.724
But precisely because it's not the kind of road

00:22:51.724 --> 00:22:54.544
where you have to stay on full alert all the time,

00:22:54.830 --> 00:22:58.661
we actually had more room to take in the changes along the way.

00:22:58.810 --> 00:23:00.530
As the altitude kept inching higher,

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:03.413
the scenery around us gradually opened up too.

00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:05.760
The wind got cooler and cooler as well.

00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:09.477
And we reached the final uphill stretch to the summit.

00:23:21.430 --> 00:23:24.645
Great traction. The traction's great today.

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:48.389
Wait, I'll help you. I'm coming.

00:23:51.173 --> 00:23:52.413
Shit, there's a chain here?

00:23:52.413 --> 00:23:53.362
It's getting wrapped up, it's getting wrapped up.

00:23:53.362 --> 00:23:55.872
Don't move, don't move, don't move.

00:23:56.600 --> 00:23:58.565
Good thing I'm wearing riding boots, or you'd be done for.

00:23:58.565 --> 00:24:00.233
Yeah, you'd be totally screwed.

00:24:00.600 --> 00:24:01.566
Nice.

00:24:11.168 --> 00:24:12.230
June, can you handle it?

00:24:15.533 --> 00:24:18.200
Okay, this is the Adventure I wanted.

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:22.426
This is the Adventure I wanted.

00:24:24.200 --> 00:24:25.933
Come on the edge people, come on the edge people.

00:24:27.566 --> 00:24:28.833
Way to go, underdog.

00:24:29.266 --> 00:24:33.500
Aaaahhhahaha!

00:24:33.660 --> 00:24:35.520
We've taken out six pineapples (crashed into them, LOL).

00:24:43.233 --> 00:24:44.300
Nice.

00:24:46.930 --> 00:24:50.656
What a view. So beautiful.

00:24:54.506 --> 00:24:56.096
Pineapple.

00:25:03.730 --> 00:25:05.808
So beautiful.

00:25:06.730 --> 00:25:08.121
Every time we come here,

00:25:08.121 --> 00:25:09.104
we give each other a hug.

00:25:12.233 --> 00:25:13.533
Nice!

00:25:14.300 --> 00:25:17.040
So tired. I made it up here on the bike.

00:25:22.966 --> 00:25:25.600
And when we finally rode up that slope,

00:25:25.933 --> 00:25:29.633
the view in front of us instantly made everyone go quiet.

00:25:29.800 --> 00:25:32.330
At the top was this endless, sweeping view.

00:25:32.698 --> 00:25:35.210
No obstructions at all, nothing getting in the way.

00:25:35.242 --> 00:25:37.482
Your sight just keeps stretching out

00:25:37.626 --> 00:25:39.621
so far it feels like there's no edge.

00:25:39.861 --> 00:25:42.138
All around us were pineapple fields

00:25:42.433 --> 00:25:44.300
laid out neatly across the hillsides.

00:25:44.560 --> 00:25:48.384
The evening light made the whole scene feel especially gentle.

00:25:48.700 --> 00:25:50.333
It was just around sunset.

00:25:50.433 --> 00:25:52.700
The sunset slowly moved toward the horizon.

00:25:52.960 --> 00:25:56.260
Golden light spilled over the hills and the fields.

00:25:56.260 --> 00:25:58.320
and it also touched every one of us.

00:25:58.576 --> 00:26:02.224
A breeze blew down from above, carrying a bit of the mountain's chill.

00:26:02.366 --> 00:26:04.200
But the view in front of us was warm.

00:26:04.266 --> 00:26:05.866
It's hard to describe that feeling.

00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:08.066
It wasn't grand, and it wasn't overwhelming.

00:26:08.330 --> 00:26:10.954
It was a quiet, deeply moving feeling.

00:26:11.200 --> 00:26:12.933
It was like after riding all this way,

00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:14.933
through the forest and along the mountain roads,

00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:18.426
through one unfamiliar scene after another, you finally arrived here.

00:26:18.600 --> 00:26:20.433
Everything suddenly felt so worth it.

00:26:20.466 --> 00:26:22.100
And what made it even more unforgettable

00:26:22.200 --> 00:26:23.898
was that after we reached the summit,

00:26:24.066 --> 00:26:26.633
Joseph gave each of us a hug.

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:28.821
That hug was really simple,

00:26:28.933 --> 00:26:30.800
but at that time, in that place,

00:26:30.848 --> 00:26:32.474
it felt especially meaningful.

00:26:32.733 --> 00:26:33.800
You'd suddenly feel

00:26:33.800 --> 00:26:35.033
that today's ride

00:26:35.166 --> 00:26:38.000
wasn't just about bringing you to see a view.

00:26:38.160 --> 00:26:41.362
It was because someone truly hoped you'd come here yourself,

00:26:41.362 --> 00:26:45.013
see these mountains, these fields, and this sunset with your own eyes,

00:26:45.233 --> 00:26:48.766
and feel for yourself what makes this trip truly special —

00:26:48.766 --> 00:26:49.900
not just the scenery,

00:26:50.208 --> 00:26:52.490
but the people around us too.

00:27:04.733 --> 00:27:08.063
There was less than half an hour left until sunset at 6:05.

00:27:08.063 --> 00:27:10.513
And now, we've arrived at this pineapple field.

00:27:10.513 --> 00:27:13.466
We rode up here from that road over there.

00:27:13.898 --> 00:27:15.930
The moment we just rode up here,

00:27:15.930 --> 00:27:19.562
seeing the whole pineapple field was incredibly, incredibly, incredibly vast.

00:27:19.562 --> 00:27:21.400
And the whole thing was so spectacular.

00:27:21.400 --> 00:27:22.866
It's really beautiful here.

00:27:22.866 --> 00:27:25.533
Especially with the sunset right now.

00:27:25.900 --> 00:27:27.463
Personally, I think it feels so poetic.

00:27:27.463 --> 00:27:29.280
Let's stay here for a bit first.

00:27:29.280 --> 00:27:30.500
Let me relax for a moment.

00:27:30.700 --> 00:27:33.033
Then we'll get ready to head down. Go!

00:27:44.933 --> 00:27:46.633
What I'm more worried about now is

00:27:46.830 --> 00:27:50.917
whether we'll be riding back in the dark when we head down later.

00:28:10.949 --> 00:28:15.440
Parked. No collision, no collision.

00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:19.317
Up on the mountain, we stayed until the sun went down

00:28:19.317 --> 00:28:21.100
before reluctantly getting ready to head back down.

00:28:21.430 --> 00:28:23.311
In the end, we rode for about another hour

00:28:23.311 --> 00:28:24.693
and finally, at 6 p.m. at night,

00:28:24.800 --> 00:28:27.008
we arrived at tonight's lodging.

00:28:32.700 --> 00:28:33.642
Good evening, everyone.

00:28:33.642 --> 00:28:35.466
This is our first night riding.

00:28:35.630 --> 00:28:38.117
Tonight we had something really special for dinner.

00:28:38.330 --> 00:28:42.405
Boodle Fight.

00:28:42.500 --> 00:28:43.422
No plates at all.

00:28:43.422 --> 00:28:44.792
The rice and all the food

00:28:44.792 --> 00:28:47.411
were all laid out on plastic wrap on the table.

00:28:47.411 --> 00:28:49.866
So how do we eat it? It's really special.

00:28:50.448 --> 00:28:52.700
First, you put on two chicken gloves.

00:28:54.256 --> 00:28:57.024
Then, then what? Just grab it?

00:28:57.024 --> 00:28:59.700
Or do we do that thing we loved as kids —

00:28:59.700 --> 00:29:01.331
mix everything together?

00:29:01.331 --> 00:29:02.474
Do you want to get hit?

00:29:02.821 --> 00:29:04.026
They have to eat too.

00:29:04.133 --> 00:29:05.884
Lord Jesus,

00:29:05.884 --> 00:29:09.004
thank You for the opportunity

00:29:09.004 --> 00:29:14.010
to ride with our friends from Taiwan,

00:29:14.010 --> 00:29:17.363
and thank You also for keeping us safe the whole time.

00:29:17.363 --> 00:29:19.491
Amen.

00:29:19.491 --> 00:29:21.600
Amen.

00:29:24.416 --> 00:29:27.230
Amen, amen, amen, amen.

00:29:27.578 --> 00:29:30.660
This is our traditional way of sharing food.

00:29:30.866 --> 00:29:34.933
In Filipino families, people eat together,

00:29:35.100 --> 00:29:38.933
so we lay out all the food and share it with our family.

00:29:39.258 --> 00:29:40.700
You are our family.

00:29:45.266 --> 00:29:46.900
Okay, then I'm going to dig in.

00:29:46.900 --> 00:29:48.966
This feels like I'm letting my wild side out.

00:29:48.966 --> 00:29:51.833
Boodle Fight isn't the name of one specific dish,

00:29:51.833 --> 00:29:53.833
it's a style of eating.

00:29:54.200 --> 00:29:57.700
The dishes, rice, and fruit are just laid out right on the table.

00:29:57.800 --> 00:29:59.066
No one uses bowls or chopsticks — it's all hands.

00:29:59.178 --> 00:30:02.080
You just grab the rice and eat it with the dishes by hand.

00:30:02.300 --> 00:30:05.813
The key is sharing, the lively atmosphere, and that easy sense of closeness.

00:30:06.066 --> 00:30:07.400
And no dishes to wash, haha.

00:30:07.400 --> 00:30:09.800
Honestly, the most interesting part of this way of eating

00:30:09.800 --> 00:30:11.931
isn't just the part about eating with your hands.

00:30:11.931 --> 00:30:14.170
It's when you're really standing there in front of that table

00:30:14.170 --> 00:30:15.717
that you can feel it very clearly.

00:30:15.829 --> 00:30:17.760
This isn't simply about eating a meal.

00:30:17.900 --> 00:30:19.978
It's more like they're using the most direct way

00:30:19.978 --> 00:30:23.333
to put their warmth, the lack of distance, and the bond between people

00:30:23.333 --> 00:30:24.766
all out on the table together.

00:30:24.900 --> 00:30:25.900
Once the utensils are gone,

00:30:25.900 --> 00:30:27.766
everything becomes much simpler.

00:30:27.766 --> 00:30:29.266
You don't have to think too much about the rules.

00:30:29.266 --> 00:30:30.966
You also won't feel too restricted.

00:30:30.966 --> 00:30:33.766
You just naturally enjoy the food and the atmosphere.

00:30:33.866 --> 00:30:35.633
Then you naturally blend into the moment.

00:30:35.633 --> 00:30:37.800
This meal really makes you feel like

00:30:37.860 --> 00:30:40.181
you're not just here in the Philippines to "see" a trip,

00:30:40.330 --> 00:30:42.880
but to actually step into their lives.

00:30:45.300 --> 00:30:47.102
And this place to stay is in the mountains.

00:30:47.102 --> 00:30:48.666
I actually think being able to find a place

00:30:48.700 --> 00:30:51.266
in the mountains that can host a whole group

00:30:51.300 --> 00:30:52.633
is really not easy.

00:30:52.700 --> 00:30:55.963
The best part is that the place is clean and tidy,

00:30:55.963 --> 00:30:57.109
and it even has a swimming pool.

00:30:57.366 --> 00:30:59.731
The overall quality of the stay is really excellent.

00:30:59.731 --> 00:31:02.789
We woke up at 6 a.m., packed our bags, and put on our gear.

00:31:02.966 --> 00:31:05.131
Before setting off, we have to grab a coffee first.

00:31:05.131 --> 00:31:06.384
Early in the morning, we start with a cup of coffee

00:31:06.384 --> 00:31:07.766
to get us energized for the whole day.

00:31:07.766 --> 00:31:09.166
Can you introduce today's itinerary?

00:31:09.733 --> 00:31:11.900
Today's itinerary is an itinerary we don't know.

00:31:16.700 --> 00:31:18.100
I'll ride up front today.

00:31:19.433 --> 00:31:20.833
Then I can take photos for you guys.

00:31:21.621 --> 00:31:23.936
Are you ready?

00:31:31.766 --> 00:31:34.563
After coffee, we happily hopped on our bikes.

00:31:34.563 --> 00:31:36.698
And we were ready to start today's adventure.

00:31:37.034 --> 00:31:39.610
Early in the morning, we kept heading east toward Tanay.

00:31:39.610 --> 00:31:40.896
Not long after we set off,

00:31:40.896 --> 00:31:42.663
the sky suddenly changed like crazy, XDDDD.

00:31:42.663 --> 00:31:44.389
A thick fog suddenly rolled in all around us.

00:31:44.566 --> 00:31:46.233
We could still see the mountains in the distance at first.

00:31:46.360 --> 00:31:49.520
In the next second, everything around us was swallowed by the fog.

00:31:49.866 --> 00:31:51.900
The road ahead started to blur.

00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:54.490
The scenery farther out almost completely disappeared.

00:31:54.630 --> 00:31:56.673
Honestly, riding a motorcycle in this kind of thick fog

00:31:56.673 --> 00:31:58.421
is really pretty thrilling.

00:31:58.645 --> 00:31:59.632
For the locals,

00:31:59.632 --> 00:32:01.833
weather like this is already cold enough to need a jacket

00:32:01.966 --> 00:32:03.200
and start saying it's chilly.

00:32:03.433 --> 00:32:05.766
But for us, it really didn't feel that way at all.

00:32:05.800 --> 00:32:06.933
We even felt like

00:32:06.933 --> 00:32:09.000
this temperature was insanely comfortable, lol.

00:32:09.300 --> 00:32:10.743
Maybe because we came from Taiwan,

00:32:10.743 --> 00:32:12.090
and because we'd been riding all the way,

00:32:12.266 --> 00:32:14.000
our bodies had already been working non-stop,

00:32:14.330 --> 00:32:18.037
so this damp, slightly cool mountain air,

00:32:18.300 --> 00:32:20.000
which honestly made it pretty fun,

00:32:20.149 --> 00:32:22.860
the wind on your body wasn't the kind of biting cold.

00:32:23.000 --> 00:32:26.333
It just added a bit more of an adventure feel to the whole trip.

00:32:26.500 --> 00:32:28.882
And because of that sudden thick fog,

00:32:28.882 --> 00:32:30.730
what was supposed to be just a simple ride

00:32:30.830 --> 00:32:32.602
suddenly became really memorable.

00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:35.600
We rode through the fog for who knows how long.

00:32:35.600 --> 00:32:38.300
When we headed back down the mountain, the weather cleared up again.

00:32:38.630 --> 00:32:42.074
And the off-road section we'd been looking forward to all day finally came around again.

00:33:27.260 --> 00:33:27.957
This dirt road

00:33:27.957 --> 00:33:31.166
was the last dirt section of our two-day ride,

00:33:31.300 --> 00:33:33.933
stretching all the way from the mountains down to the coast.

00:33:33.933 --> 00:33:35.400
And at the very start of this section,

00:33:35.568 --> 00:33:38.298
it immediately gave me major East Malaysia riding vibes.

00:33:38.460 --> 00:33:39.744
There were a lot of straight stretches.

00:33:39.744 --> 00:33:41.131
The visibility was really far too.

00:33:41.131 --> 00:33:43.626
The road was covered with a thin layer of tiny gravel.

00:33:43.900 --> 00:33:45.081
That feeling when you ride on it?

00:33:45.081 --> 00:33:46.528
Honestly, pure joy.

00:33:46.666 --> 00:33:48.833
If you want to stand up, just stand and ride.

00:33:48.833 --> 00:33:49.963
If you wanna drift a little side to side,

00:33:49.963 --> 00:33:52.389
you can loosen up a bit and just ride and slide around.

00:33:52.533 --> 00:33:55.400
Anyway, once you got onto this road, it kept giving me the feeling

00:33:55.400 --> 00:33:58.300
that this road was basically made for playing around on bikes.

00:33:58.533 --> 00:34:00.500
The gravel kept sliding under the tires,

00:34:00.500 --> 00:34:04.069
that loose, slippery feeling where you can still control the line

00:34:04.166 --> 00:34:06.166
really makes you get more and more addicted the more you ride.

00:34:06.166 --> 00:34:09.333
But this wasn't the kind of place where you could completely zone out either.

00:34:09.430 --> 00:34:10.602
Because you never knew

00:34:10.602 --> 00:34:13.833
whether a car might suddenly appear in the oncoming lane the next second.

00:34:13.833 --> 00:34:16.000
Sometimes just a second ago you were still enjoying that

00:34:16.000 --> 00:34:18.200
endless straightaway rush,

00:34:18.384 --> 00:34:21.130
and the next second you have to quickly tuck back in.

00:34:21.233 --> 00:34:23.966
Another thing here that really left an impression on me

00:34:23.966 --> 00:34:26.600
was just how many huge puddles there were on the road.

00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:29.633
At first, I instinctively wanted to dodge every single one.

00:34:29.808 --> 00:34:31.632
After all, if you can avoid getting wet, you should.

00:34:31.786 --> 00:34:33.850
If you can stay clean, stay clean.

00:34:34.021 --> 00:34:35.631
But as the ride went on,

00:34:35.631 --> 00:34:37.498
Joseph kept splashing water on me too, XDDD.

00:34:37.700 --> 00:34:38.933
Every time I hit a puddle,

00:34:38.960 --> 00:34:40.784
I got a little more mud on me.

00:34:40.930 --> 00:34:43.024
In the end, I completely gave up resisting.

00:34:43.130 --> 00:34:47.168
I just went into a "fine, whatever, bring it on" mode.

00:34:47.360 --> 00:34:49.274
If I saw a puddle, I just went straight through it.

00:34:49.520 --> 00:34:50.090
That said,

00:34:50.090 --> 00:34:51.509
once you stop worrying about getting wet,

00:34:51.509 --> 00:34:53.500
you stop thinking about how to avoid it

00:34:53.500 --> 00:34:54.966
or how to stay clean.

00:34:55.125 --> 00:34:58.304
Riding suddenly gets a whole lot more fun.

00:35:10.661 --> 00:35:13.754
In the end, we rode this dirt road for nearly an hour and a half,

00:35:13.860 --> 00:35:16.944
all the way until our planned stop time.

00:35:17.194 --> 00:35:19.104
Even though we didn't make it all the way through,

00:35:19.104 --> 00:35:20.672
that's just how travel is sometimes.

00:35:20.760 --> 00:35:23.574
You don't always have to ride every road to the very end.

00:35:23.574 --> 00:35:24.890
Sometimes leaving a little regret

00:35:25.093 --> 00:35:28.500
keeps that unfinished stretch lingering in your mind,

00:35:28.640 --> 00:35:29.952
gives you more room to imagine,

00:35:30.100 --> 00:35:33.200
and gives you another reason to come back.

00:35:33.200 --> 00:35:34.862
After wrapping up the morning ride,

00:35:34.862 --> 00:35:36.490
we had a simple lunch,

00:35:36.500 --> 00:35:38.566
then rode another 3.5 hours

00:35:38.640 --> 00:35:39.968
all the way back to Manila.

00:35:41.946 --> 00:35:43.311
After we got back to Manila,

00:35:43.311 --> 00:35:44.800
then it was dinner time.

00:35:44.928 --> 00:35:46.921
The moment everyone sat down to eat,

00:35:46.921 --> 00:35:48.794
the atmosphere was actually especially relaxed.

00:35:48.860 --> 00:35:52.592
It felt like, "Ah, today's ride was really worth it."

00:35:52.592 --> 00:35:55.200
Even though we were still a little dusty,

00:35:55.200 --> 00:35:56.642
what stayed in our heads

00:35:56.642 --> 00:35:58.944
was all the scenery from the past two days on the road.

00:35:59.024 --> 00:35:59.742
Thoughts?

00:35:59.742 --> 00:36:00.981
Why so sudden?

00:36:01.904 --> 00:36:03.344
Buy a bike, find Xiao Rou.

00:36:09.090 --> 00:36:10.960
For tire changes, should we go with Pirelli?

00:36:12.853 --> 00:36:14.400
It was a blast riding. Let's come again next time.

00:36:16.554 --> 00:36:18.624
Anyone who wants to turn back, ride in front of me, lol.

00:36:21.300 --> 00:36:25.226
Hit me up if you wanna ride.

00:36:27.061 --> 00:36:31.024
Ride hard, eat well, drink well. Nobody turn back.

00:36:33.300 --> 00:36:36.421
Bring more Taiwanese people to the Philippines to get their licenses.

00:36:38.250 --> 00:36:39.221
Nice.

00:36:40.300 --> 00:36:44.768
I hope we can have an all-road Philippines ride trip someday.

00:36:44.768 --> 00:36:47.762
A city riding trip.

00:36:47.762 --> 00:36:49.456
Aren't we here for dirt roads?

00:36:49.733 --> 00:36:52.500
Wait, don't you think city riding is even harder than dirt roads?

00:36:52.922 --> 00:36:53.253
Fun.

00:36:53.253 --> 00:36:55.433
But we can unleash our wild side.

00:36:58.100 --> 00:37:00.394
Thanks to Lu-te for inviting us this time.

00:37:00.730 --> 00:37:03.941
This was our second overseas ride with them.

00:37:03.941 --> 00:37:06.300
Keep chasing our dreams.

00:37:06.300 --> 00:37:07.931
Ride in every country.

00:37:07.931 --> 00:37:10.288
Awesome~

00:37:10.288 --> 00:37:11.466
As long as we're happy.

00:37:13.968 --> 00:37:16.913
This trip went on in such a fun and fulfilling atmosphere

00:37:16.913 --> 00:37:19.626
and slowly came to a… comma, XD.

00:37:20.033 --> 00:37:20.833
Manila,

00:37:21.100 --> 00:37:23.466
I'll be back soon!!!

00:37:25.500 --> 00:37:27.408
Today we've come to the last day of the trip.

00:37:27.408 --> 00:37:28.866
We're about to get on a plane and head home.

00:37:28.866 --> 00:37:32.533
And right now we're at the SM mall,

00:37:33.030 --> 00:37:35.349
eating this local McDonald's in the Philippines.

00:37:35.349 --> 00:37:36.900
When we were ordering, none of us noticed,

00:37:36.900 --> 00:37:39.500
then after we ordered, we realized the kids' meal here comes with this.

00:37:39.866 --> 00:37:41.033
And we just got three.

00:37:41.033 --> 00:37:42.466
One is, what, Psyduck?

00:37:42.560 --> 00:37:44.218
And the other one is also Psyduck?

00:37:45.466 --> 00:37:47.200
Ready to battle it out — we're going to buy ten sets.

00:37:47.200 --> 00:37:48.597
We went just for this ball.

00:37:48.741 --> 00:37:50.200
We can't even finish the rest of the food.

00:37:50.266 --> 00:37:51.666
We'll just give them away to random people.

00:37:51.666 --> 00:37:52.200
Let's go.

00:37:52.200 --> 00:37:53.600
My target is just this one.

00:37:53.700 --> 00:37:54.666
This is Pichu.

00:37:54.666 --> 00:37:55.700
Ah, they don't have Pikachu?

00:37:55.700 --> 00:37:56.600
They didn't put it here.

00:37:56.660 --> 00:37:58.032
Lucario is pretty cool too.

00:38:03.109 --> 00:38:05.312
Hopefully I can draw Pikachu.

00:38:34.160 --> 00:38:36.021
Bye-bye, bye-bye, bye-bye.

00:38:36.666 --> 00:38:37.966
It's mostly Poké Balls.

00:38:39.200 --> 00:38:41.866
So stoked — I get to unbox a bunch of blind boxes.

00:38:43.300 --> 00:38:47.731
Pika — this is all for this one.

00:38:47.731 --> 00:38:50.272
1:02 a.m.,

00:38:50.272 --> 00:38:51.431
we finally made it back to Taiwan.

00:38:51.431 --> 00:38:54.864
We pulled a Pikachu — awesome!

00:39:53.109 --> 00:39:54.650
Alright, that's the end of today's video.

00:39:54.650 --> 00:39:56.433
If you liked this video after watching it,

00:39:56.433 --> 00:39:57.666
don't forget to

00:39:57.733 --> 00:39:59.366
like, subscribe, comment, and share.

00:39:59.366 --> 00:40:00.200
I'm Rut.

00:40:00.300 --> 00:40:03.433
See you next time, bye-bye~

